# ============================================================
# 5. HOW TO RUN THIS AUTOMATICALLY FOR SEVERAL WEEKS
# ============================================================
#
# OPTION A — Windows (Task Scheduler):
#   1. Open "Task Scheduler" (search in the Start Menu)
#   2. Create Task -> name it "TrafficDataCollection"
#   3. Triggers tab -> New -> select "Daily", Repeat task every "15 minutes"
#      for a duration of "Indefinitely"
#   4. Actions tab -> New -> Program/script: path to python.exe
#      Arguments: full path to collect_traffic_data.py
#      (e.g. C:\Users\you\Desktop\collect_traffic_data.py)
#   5. Save. The machine must stay on and not sleep for this to run on schedule.
#
# OPTION B — Mac/Linux (cron):
#   1. Open Terminal, type: crontab -e
#   2. Add this line (runs every 15 minutes):
#      */15 * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /path/to/collect_traffic_data.py
#   3. Save and exit.
#
# OPTION C — Simplest option if you don't have a machine running 24/7
#   (collect only while you're studying):
#   Use the companion script collect_traffic_data_loop.py — it loops
#   automatically inside Python, just leave it running while you want
#   to collect data.
# ============================================================